BEHAVIOR array-buf-size

DESCRIPTION
  Bytes a caller must provide to back an int array of `cap` 8-byte elements:
  16-byte header ([len:8][cap:8]) + cap*8 data. Use it to size the MEMORY
  region (or any caller-owned buffer) that array-* operates on.

CONTRACT
  INPUT cap int 8
  OUTPUT size int 8
  GUARANTEES pure no_alloc writes_output

HASH 694a01ba

IMPLEMENTATION
  cv = LOAD cap 8
  e = IMUL cv 8 8
  s = IADD e 16 8
  STORE size s 8
END
